{"assets":["/statement-assets/d6370f9ca4df167dec8f6f05e858f4e3f52157c21c771aa95e3fc35df64e5eb3.png","/statement-assets/c1bcc272de2de980b21d636ad62a9e282db802a800e141d1d4f6c16ffe05ad17.png","/statement-assets/c7fbf2246d838faaa2fffb826888a067e86863052041e0eeb1f0ca4205246991.png","/statement-assets/17e93e6c988a80c7f7e83aa971b4a54b7df107d66acb221590a0508cfa08875c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"768","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Code For 1"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Jon fought bravely to rescue the wildlings who were attacked by the white-walkers at Hardhome. On his arrival, Sam tells him that he wants to go to Oldtown to train at the Citadel to become a maester, so he can return and take the deceased Aemon's place as maester of Castle Black. Jon agrees to Sam's proposal and Sam sets off his journey to the Citadel. However becoming a trainee at the Citadel is not a cakewalk and hence the maesters at the Citadel gave Sam a problem to test his eligibility. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially Sam has a list with a single element "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then he has to perform certain operations on this list. In each operation Sam must remove any element "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x > 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", from the list and insert at the same position "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d6370f9ca4df167dec8f6f05e858f4e3f52157c21c771aa95e3fc35df64e5eb3.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c1bcc272de2de980b21d636ad62a9e282db802a800e141d1d4f6c16ffe05ad17.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d6370f9ca4df167dec8f6f05e858f4e3f52157c21c771aa95e3fc35df64e5eb3.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" sequentially. He must continue with these operations until all the elements in the list are either "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now the masters want the total number of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"s in the range "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"-indexed). Sam wants to become a maester but unfortunately he cannot solve this problem. Can you help Sam to pass the eligibility test?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ n < 250"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ r - l ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r ≥ 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l ≥ 1"},{"kind":"text","text":") – initial element and the range "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not greater than the length of the final list."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the total number of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"s in the range "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the final sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 3 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider first example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c7fbf2246d838faaa2fffb826888a067e86863052041e0eeb1f0ca4205246991.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Elements on positions from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"-nd to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th in list is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[1, 1, 1, 1]"},{"kind":"text","text":". The number of ones is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/17e93e6c988a80c7f7e83aa971b4a54b7df107d66acb221590a0508cfa08875c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Elements on positions from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":"-rd to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th in list is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0]"},{"kind":"text","text":". The number of ones is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"768B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/768/problem/B"}